{#- Renders every enabled MegooPM whitelist as one multi-document parser file.

    CrowdSec reads `---`-separated documents in a single parser file as separate
    nodes (verified on v1.6.4: a two-whitelist file logs "Loaded 2 parser
    nodes"). Scalars go through `tojson` because JSON is a subset of YAML: it
    quotes and escapes correctly whatever the operator typed, so a reason or an
    expression containing `:` or `#` cannot break the file — and a parser file
    CrowdSec cannot load stops it starting, which with APPSEC_FAILURE_ACTION=deny
    means every protected host fails closed.

    Each document renders only its own kind's keys. That is not cosmetic:
    CrowdSec evaluates every key it finds, so an `ip:` list left on an
    expression whitelist would silently widen it.

    Whitespace is controlled so identical input renders byte-identical output;
    the digest of this file decides whether CrowdSec is restarted at all. -#}
# Managed by MegooPM — do not edit by hand.
{% for doc in docs %}---
name: {{ ("megoopm/wl-" ~ doc.slug) | yamlstr }}
description: {{ doc.description | yamlstr }}
{%- if doc.is_expression and doc.filter %}
filter: {{ doc.filter | yamlstr }}
{%- endif %}
whitelist:
  reason: {{ doc.reason | yamlstr }}
{%- if doc.is_expression %}
  expression:
{%- for expression in doc.expressions %}
    - {{ expression | yamlstr }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- else %}
{%- if doc.ips %}
  ip:
{%- for ip in doc.ips %}
    - {{ ip | yamlstr }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
{%- if doc.cidrs %}
  cidr:
{%- for cidr in doc.cidrs %}
    - {{ cidr | yamlstr }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
{% endfor -%}
